101	6.0.7 - 08/17/26
102	----------------
103	
104	- JavaScript library symbols can now use the `__force` and `__export`
105	  decorators to control inclusion and export visibility. (#27436)
106	- contrib.glfw3 port upgraded to use the latest version of GLFW 3.5.1
107	  (#27508)
108	- `-fwasm-exceptions` now links the Wasm EH runtime (libunwind and the
109	  `__cpp_exception` tag) independently of C++ linking, so Wasm EH objects from
110	  non-C++ frontends (e.g. rustc, which links via `emcc`) link without
111	  requiring `em++` or `-sDEFAULT_TO_CXX`. (#27496)
112	- FreeType was updated to 2.14.3 (#27518)
113	- The oldest supported Safari version (`MIN_SAFARI_VERSION`) was raised from
114	  14.1 to 15.0, making 15.0 the minimum version that can be targeted. This
115	  allows assuming `bulk-memory`, `nontrapping-fptoint`, and `WASM_BIGINT`
116	  (`JS_BIGINT_INTEGRATION`) are universally available across all supported
117	  engines, and removes legacy JS polyfills and Binaryen lowering passes.
118	  (#27542)
119	
120	6.0.6 - 08/05/26
121	----------------
122	- `DEFAULT_TO_CXX` is now disabled by default. This means that `em++` is now
123	  required when linking C++ programs, matching the behavior of clang and gcc.
124	  The old behavior is still available using `-sDEFAULT_TO_CXX`. (#11121)
125	- Added example Meson cross compilation files (`wasm32-emscripten.ini` and
126	  `wasm64-emscripten.ini`) in `tools/meson/`. (#27478)
127	- libcxx and libcxxabi were updated to LLVM 22.1.8. (#27428)
128	
129	6.0.5 - 07/29/26
